00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:49.170
Uh, basically turbo tax, uh, that would have,
among other things restricted the IRS from

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:53.820
creating its own sort of government tax filing
system.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.820
Right?

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:55.820
That's exactly right.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:01:00.040
And we, uh, so, uh, Richard Neal, who's the
congressman here in Massachusetts has been

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:04.330
involved with this and sort of sadly, I mean,
I like the guy personally and he was like

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:08.540
the first when I started doing this show,
the first sort of real elected official that

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:09.680
I ever met.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:14.350
Uh, but I'm not particularly thrilled with
his role in this and it's not necessarily

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:15.350
a unique role.

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:20.460
I mean, this is actually relatively uncontroversial
